# Cursor Rules for WBAT iTerm2 Status Bar

## Code Style
- Use Python 3.9+ features
- Follow PEP 8 style guide
- Line length: 100 characters (configured in pyproject.toml)
- Use type hints where appropriate
- Format code with `black` before committing
- Run `ruff check` to catch linting issues

## Formatting
- Always format code with `black` before committing
- Run `ruff check --fix` to auto-fix linting issues
- Use `black src/ tests/` to format all Python files
- Use `ruff check src/ tests/` to check for issues

## Testing
- Write tests for new features
- Run tests with `pytest tests/`
- Ensure all tests pass before committing

## Code Quality
- Keep functions focused and small
- Use descriptive variable names
- Add docstrings to public functions/classes
- Handle errors gracefully with appropriate logging
- Use async/await for I/O operations

## Dependencies
- Keep dependencies minimal
- Document why each dependency is needed
- Use type hints for better IDE support

## Git
- Write clear commit messages
- Keep commits focused on a single change
- Run formatting and linting before committing
